<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12216"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Megabyte<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Megabyte<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 25, 2005 - 12:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here are some tips if you plan on going to one of Beattie&#39;s signings:  <BR><b>1.Make sure you have your name on a sticky note on the front cover so Robert can sign &#34;To: So and so&#34;.</b> <BR><b>2.Get there an hour early, it helps, because you possibly could be the first one in line.</b><!--/Text--></td></tr>
