<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13135"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brady<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brady<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 23, 2005 - 9:49 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I just finished the book - I&#39;m happy to send it to someone if they want it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13135-->
<!--Post: 13141--><!--Time: 1114305148-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13141"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 23, 2005 - 6:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->pg 256 &#34;What intervened in the Green River Killer investigation was unbelieveable police stupidity that has NOT been seen in the BTK investigation.&#34; <BR> <BR>Beattie stated this because he felt that LE should have tested a sample of DNA, obtained from Ridgeway in 1987, they had on Ridgeway. The police did not test as they were afraid that they did not have enough material to test a second time. B goes onto say that it was a mistake.  .  .   <BR> <BR>My point ?  Why is our &#34;lawyer&#34; so honest about this possbile mistake yet he conveniently omits any mistakes or wrong doing by the WPD ????? <BR> <BR>The answer is right in the text. Beattie list detectives and journalists he has had long standing relationships with and he outlines his standing in the Wichita community.  .  .  <BR> <BR>If I had done my own due diligence, read a chapter at a Borders Book store before buying, I would have known that this guy is a self serving, egotistical, shill producing unfounded praise for many of the people that made crucial mistakes that allowed BTK to kill for 30&#43; years.  .  .   <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13141-->
<!--Post: 13142--><!--Time: 1114305683-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13142"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 23, 2005 - 6:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Elsewhere <BR> <BR>Thank you for the support. I too believe that Rader had either a life changing event or something else that goaded him to contact police.  .  .   <BR> <BR>Unlike the tone that Beattie sets, I believe that BTK has killed the entire 30&#43; years he has been free. <BR> <BR>BTW to Beattie or any Beattie advocates, can anyone explain why the WPD, according to Beattie, ignored BTK &#34;like&#34; M.O. murders during the years BTK went silent ? <BR> <BR>Beattie states that almost all LE told him that BTK was either dead, encarcerated, or in a mental institution.  .  .  yet Beattie never criticized or spoke out against these LE &#34;assumptions&#34; <BR> <BR>Yet again Beattie was ready and willing to pile on the Seattle area LE and give his &#34;analysis &amp; opinion&#34; on their performance even though he clearly states that he will &#34;only document and present&#34; the events throughout the BTK investigation ????????? <BR> <BR>That smacks of severe favoritism.  .  .  and Ivy although I agree with the idea that the writing mechanics were infantile &#40;my word&#41;, I think the greater more disturbing issue is that Beattie seems to be &#34;protecting&#34; or &#34;deflecting&#34; critisism of LE in the BTK case.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13142-->
<!--Post: 13143--><!--Time: 1114305955-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13143"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 23, 2005 - 6:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve, <BR> <BR>I greatly respect your opinions on this site as well as the Zodiac site. I appreciate your support and you have a wonderful velvet glove way of presenting issues.  .  .   <BR> <BR>I on the other hand am more like the knuckle dragging neanderthal ready to drop the hammer on such obviously biased writing.  <BR> <BR>Your method is much more effective.  .  .  mine allows me to vent the dissatisfaction/venom of a person who feels he has been &#34;bamboozled&#34; out of his $14.00 bucks US.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13143-->
<!--Post: 13151--><!--Time: 1114314139-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13151"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:williammichael@direcway.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 23, 2005 - 8:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have yet to read the book, but I suspect there are additional reasons for Beattie &#34;going easy&#34; on the WPD.  Not only does he have friends and associates in the LE and DA&#39;s offices but he plans to publish a 2nd addition after the trial and probably hopes to interview Rader, etc.  He fears criticising LE as all his sources for the future writing would cut him out of the loop.  He is probably right on target with this belief.  WPD is NEVER going to admit making any mistakes and any expose&#39; will have to be written by someone who does not care if Sedgewick County authorities like the writer or ever speak to them again.  Let us hope some writer takes on the challenge.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13151-->
<!--Post: 13154--><!--Time: 1114347037-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13154"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tulip<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tulip<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, April 24, 2005 - 5:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I will repeat what I said in any earlier post regarding Beattie&#39;s treatment of WPD: <BR> <BR>IMO, Beattie did an outstanding job at making WPD look good by saying how many man hours were spent, stories of the &#34;extraordinary measures&#34; like the satelite photos, but at the same time he discreetly pointed out their many incomprehensible mistakes. I think he did this intentionally. He doesn&#39;t want to alienate any of his sources in LE, but he still wants the story told.  <BR> <BR>It seemed to me that over and over again, they were refusing to admit that a serial killer could be involved in the killings. I guess I was expecting to find out that they were downplaying BTK to the public, but behind the scenes they were on top of it. Not so. There was continued debate over whether the letters were hoaxes. They did not seem to be conecting the dots.  <BR> <BR>After Vian&#39;s murder Detective Cocking said, &#34;this looks like BTK&#34;. He was immediately scorned and told to &#34;Knock off that sh&#42;&#42;.&#34;  <BR> <BR>After Wegerle&#39;s murder, the Ghostbusters were consulted. Could this be a BTK hit? &#34;They were unanimous in agreement: No.&#34; The conclusion was made &#34;that the husband did it&#34;. They were not looking for another killer. They felt like they had their man.  <BR> <BR>One of the most shocking things I read &#40;p.236&#41;- was referring to a breakfast Beattie had with a group of retired WPO on March 23, 2004. Jack Bruce said regarding the elder Joseph Otero, &#34;The ropes on Joseph were the only ones that he could have tied himself. ... Prove that Joseph Otero didn&#39;t murder his family then kill himself, either accidentally or on purpose.&#34; Beattie continues &#34;As we departed, Bruce told me that he agreed with Floyd Hannon. He didn&#39;t think there was a BTK.&#34; This was in 2004 and some WPD still don&#39;t think there is a BTK? <BR> <BR>These are just some of the many mistakes the WPD made that are pointed out by Beattie.  IMO, as long as the facts stated in the book are accuate, I could care less what kind of spin Beatties wants to put on it.  I have a mind of my own and can make my own opinion about the kind of job WPD did based on the actions they took with the information they had.   <BR> <BR>My conclusion is there were many incomrehensible mistakes made throughout the investigation up to and including the press conference after the arrest.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13154-->
<!--Post: 13155--><!--Time: 1114374050-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13155"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, April 24, 2005 - 1:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->OK Mike, <BR> <BR>Ahmen brother ! Very astute of you as I never thought of the possibility of a 2nd Beattie book.  .  .   <BR> <BR>I think that you are correct that Beattie does not wish to piss off LE but by taking this tack he becomes the ultimate &#34;biased&#34; source of NOT information but propaganda.  .  .   <BR> <BR>Tidbits like the following on page 276 &#34;Former BTK lead investigator Bernie Drowatzky, the OLD FRIEND OF MY PARENTS who had been the detective to retrieve the very first BTK from the textbook in the Wichita Public Library in 1974.  .  .   <BR> <BR>How can we take this guy serious ? His &#34;mission statement&#34; at the beginning of the book is to document the events of the BTK case without adding his opinion or theories.  .  . yet Beattie hammers the Green River investigators adding opinion and theory. <BR> <BR>How can we take Beattie serious as a unbiased writer when his parents are life long friends to BTK investigators ? <BR> <BR>Beattie makes Robert Graysmith look down right legitimate.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13155-->
<!--Post: 13156--><!--Time: 1114374708-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13156"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, April 24, 2005 - 1:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tulip, <BR> <BR>Great point ! I too was astonished there were BTK detectives, according to Beattie, who actually took the stance that BTK did NOT even exist ! <BR> <BR>As I become more knowledgeable about this case it is obvious that the WPD made multiple and significant mistakes.  .  .   <BR> <BR>But even worse it seems that there are instances where detectives and LE did not wish to acknowledge BTK after he stopped communicating. As if they just ignored him and did not talk about him, BTK might just go away.  <BR> <BR>In the meantime BTK most likely was killing without communicating to the police ala the Zodiac. <BR> <BR>I had forgotten about how Cocking was reprimanded for noting that Vian&#39;s murder had BTK&#39;s MO.  <BR> <BR>Why the cover up ? Why were some detectives voicing their opinion that BTK was still killing while others seemed to not want to investigate the obvious BTK signs ??? <BR> <BR>I guess the better question is for Mr. Beattie. Why didn&#39;t the author, with his close familial connections to WPD &amp; LE follow up this very CONSPIRATORIAL smelling mess ??? <BR> <BR>The sad fact is that Beattie had the perfect pedigree to write a very poignant expose on the investigation. <BR> <BR>Alas Beattie was afraid lose his LE friends, contacts, and he probably feared losing his place in the community if he were to have uncovered answers to so many disturbing unanswered questions.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13156-->
<!--Post: 13163--><!--Time: 1114442169-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13163"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 25, 2005 - 8:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Beattie clearly states that he has no intention of writing a book &#34;about&#34; BTK.  AND makes it very clear in this current book that it is about the &#34;investigation&#34; only.  I think he has every intention about writing a book &#34;about&#34; BTK.  That is why there is no real critisism about the horendous mistakes along with, the conspiratorial mess of WPD...only a few minor slams...and those slams are towards specific inidviduals...Lamonyon for one...I bet his book &#34;about&#34; BTK&#34; is allready in the works. <BR>$$$$$$$$$$$$$$<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13163-->
<!--Post: 13183--><!--Time: 1114479954-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13183"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 25, 2005 - 6:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Elsewhere, <BR> <BR>Are you kidding ? You honestly believe the only reason our Mensa author did not document the WPD many glaring mistakes was simply because this book was not &#34;about BTK&#34; ??? <BR> <BR>What Beattie aka Mr. Mensa &#34;claimed&#34; his book was about was a honest documentation of the &#34;events&#34; of the BTK case over the past 30&#43; years.  .  .   <BR> <BR>Mr. Mensa claimed he would not analyze or theorize about the case.  .  . just present the facts of the case.  .  .   <BR> <BR>Guess what ?  He failed. Beattie criticized the Seattle area police investigators and their actions toward the Green River case.  <BR> <BR>Beattie criticized and editorialized a number of issue within his book.  .  .   <BR> <BR>But the worst most utterly ridiculous concept of this book is that it is being written by a bonafide &#34;unbiased&#34; &#34;authority&#34; &#40;Beattie&#41; of the BTK case.  .  .   <BR> <BR>Beattie is so biased and sympathetic toward his family friends who are detectives or his friends in the media that anything he writes must be considered tainted and viewed as less than honest work. <BR> <BR>I guarantee that the only people who will be buying a 2nd book from Beattie will be his cronies, Mensa friends, and Wichitans. <BR> <BR>People who understand the flaws and ommissions of the first book won&#39;t drop a dime for a 2nd work of trash.  .  .   <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13183-->
<!--Post: 13195--><!--Time: 1114526442-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13195"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 26, 2005 - 7:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Good point Tac.  But I was just meaning...as he so clearly stated in his book &#34;this book is not &#34;about&#34; BTK - &#40;the person&#41; I do think he will write a book &#40;probably in the works&#41; about the &#34;devil&#34; inside BTK - the REAL Dennis. <BR>But ALL of you statements are soooooooooooooo true...you are so well spoken. <BR>AND I agree - about the only people that would buy his second book....especially the main part of that group will be the &#34;High IQ&#34; cult. <BR>Thanks Tac. <BR>You have such great insight! <BR>And you also express my feelings that I have a hard time putting in writing! <BR>Thanks for speaking for me<IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13195-->
<!--Post: 13289--><!--Time: 1114810362-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13289"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 29, 2005 - 2:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Elsewhere, <BR> <BR>The last few pages are another slobber fest by Beattie where he sites other people&#39;s purported statements that this book was the cause behind Rader communicating again with press and LE.  <BR> <BR>Beattie hammers the reader with the same message over and over: his writing prompted Rader to surface and WPD caught him.  .  .   <BR> <BR>Uh that&#39;s a joke.  .  .  <BR> <BR>In fact that notion is as corny and self serving as Beattie mentioning every little mom and pop diner he frequents in Wichita.  .  .   <BR> <BR>It seems like he is attempting to prop up these restaurants for publicity sake. Undoubtedly he knows the owners and is hopefull of a free meal or 3.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13289-->
<!--Post: 13303--><!--Time: 1114844954-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13303"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 30, 2005 - 12:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>&#34;...I on the other hand am more like the knuckle dragging neanderthal ready to drop the hammer on such obviously biased writing...&#34;</i> <BR> <BR>Tac, that was beautiful. You go ahead and drag. I did cut Beattie slack, I admit. But I also gotta admit some really good points are being brought up on this thread. Glad I got around to it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13303-->
<!--Post: 13319--><!--Time: 1114971953-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13319"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, May 01, 2005 - 11:25 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve h, <BR> <BR>No problem as it is tough to keep up with all the threads.  .  . many times I have senior moments and forget where I have posted my &#34;critically important&#34; garbaaage.  <BR> <BR> <BR>One last drag and this one&#39;s for you Steve.  .  .  if a reader takes in the last few pages of Beattie&#39;s &#34;work&#34; pages 320 &amp; 321 a person has all of the evidence needed to understand why this is a work of propaganda driven by a publicity craving lawyer turned writer. <BR> <BR>Beattie sites 5 different people who believe that his book and/or the publicity surrounding his book was the reason that BTK began to communcate with LE. <BR> <BR>How perfectly self serving ! How wonderfully pathetic !! <BR> <BR>This is the same author who claims that he will not &#34;analyze the case&#34; nor will this book perform <BR>any other function than to document the events of the case. <BR> <BR>Yet here we are at the end having endured his opinions and theories on why Green River investigators &#34;failed&#34;.  <BR> <BR>We endured his opinion without evidence or even theory that the Wichita Police and LE did NOT fail in their 30&#43; years investigating the case.  <BR> <BR>And the final coup de grace we get this list of people who crown Beattie king as the sole source and reason why BTK communicated with LE and was &#34;caught by LE&#34;. <BR> <BR>Anyone with half a brain, who has put in even pedestrian levels of study, understand: <BR> <BR>1.WPD made huge mistakes  <BR>2.WPD did NOT capture BTK. . . BTK captured himself. <BR>3.Beattie mentions anyone, everyone, and every business &#40;diners etc.&#41; he has either an interest in or a familial connection.  <BR> <BR>4.The propaganda of Beattie&#39;s friends web site is such a biased account that it ignores this site and it&#39;s far superior content.  .  .  <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
