<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13407"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lizzie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lizzie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, May 04, 2005 - 8:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I just finished the book and unless he wrote it over and over, I would have never guessed he was MENSA either. I did notice that in the very last section of his book, he tried to refer to Shirley Relford as Relford, though it is Vian throughout the rest of the book. I also noticed that in BTK&#39;s letter claiming responsibility for the Oteros, he noted that Joe had a rib injury from a wreck the week before. I don&#39;t recall reading that info before the book and it sounds as though indeed if DTDC didn&#39;t have anything to do with the rib injury, he had probably been watching the Oteros closely for a while. Also, what in the hell is a death&#39;s head that beattie refers to on Steven Relford&#39;s hat? A skull or a grim reaper? maybe Death&#39;s head is a MENSA term. I also noticed at the very end Beattie thanks the book&#39;s editor, who also has worked with Carlton Smith on a Green River book. That book was horrible and hard to read, IMO. I would have rather edited the book myself. And yes, Beattie talks about himself too much in this book, congratulating himself. Does anyone know if he made the book 333 pages because of BTK&#39;s thing for 3&#39;s? It is my understanding that both the paperback and hardback books are 333 pages.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
