<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13409"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lizzie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lizzie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, May 04, 2005 - 8:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sorry about the Otero letter comment, I saw Tom premiered that here, I forgot when i read the book. I am having a hard time understanding why the WPD stored all of the evidence from these unsolved cases so poorly. I also got the impression that they had tested the envelope in a recent BTK communication for DNA &#40;I guess where he licked it&#41; and that was how they knew the new communications were from BTK himself.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
